# Personal fork — never PR upstream

This repo is Jesse's personal fork of [houssamouhra/zsh-config](https://github.com/houssamouhra/zsh-config). The original author does **not** want changes from this fork.

## Remotes

| Remote | Repo | Allowed |
|---|---|---|
| `origin` | `jessegoodier/zsh-config` | fetch, push, PRs |
| `upstream` | `houssamouhra/zsh-config` | fetch / cherry-pick only |

## Never

- Open a pull request against `houssamouhra/zsh-config` (or any other original-author remote)
- `git push` to `upstream`
- Use `gh pr create` without an explicit `--repo jessegoodier/zsh-config`

Local git may have `gh-resolved = base` on `upstream`, which makes `gh` treat the original repo as the PR base. Always override:

```bash
gh pr create --repo jessegoodier/zsh-config --title "..." --body "..."
```

## Allowed

- Fetch `upstream` and inspect commits this fork is behind on
- Cherry-pick or port selected upstream changes **into this repo**
- Open PRs on `jessegoodier/zsh-config` only
